+ Performed an initial interpretationo of the results.

Currently, we have only completed up to point five. Whilst this means we are behind schedule, our choice to include week
8 as a flexible week means we should be able to recover and return to being on schedule by the start of week 9 which
will give us ample time to write the report and create the poster.

Our primary delay was mainly caused by a need to refine and narrow our scope. Initially we intended to test a wider
variety of algorithms on a larger set of independent variables. However, after reviewing feedback for our proposal, we
undertook further research to narrow our scope to create a more useful comparison between algorithms. This reduction
will also allow us to perform a more specific experiment that could still produce novel results.

We believe our algorithm implementations are satisfactory in replicating the expected behaviour of each algorithm. While
the testing framework was developed quite quickly, this was at the expense of thorough documentation, which caused
further delay as development time went to understanding how best to use the framework for each algoithm. We are also yet
to define steps to ensure correctness for both the framework and the algorithms. To alleviate this, we plan spend the
first half of week 8 researching and reviewing our reference papers, and consulting our mentor to see how we can ensure
correctness, which will allow us to confidently move forward with experimental tests.
